gogpu/naga is an independent Go implementation of a WGSL shader compiler. It is
built on the design of Rust naga, part of the gfx-rs/wgpu project
(MIT OR Apache-2.0). This file records the reference version we started from,
what we check against, and which files are derived from Rust naga's code.

Design reference at the start
  Repository: https://github.com/gfx-rs/wgpu
  Path:       naga/
  Commit:     90db08157ccd5a5a25564219f294d023d4253d5a (2025-12-06)
  Version:    wgpu 27.0.0 (naga shares the workspace version)
  Notes:      reference code downloaded on 2025-12-07.

Files derived from Rust naga's code
  wgsl/internal/lower/conversion.go  <- naga/src/front/wgsl/lower/conversion.rs
  Copyright (c) The gfx-rs developers, MIT License:
  third_party/gfx-rs-naga/LICENSE.MIT.

Test corpus
  snapshot/testdata/rust/ vendors Rust naga's WGSL test inputs, test parameters
  and reference outputs verbatim, with their LICENSE.MIT and LICENSE.APACHE.
  Pinned to gfx-rs/wgpu 14328f49918cce19f7cc8bf703435968c8293035 (2026-10-14,
  naga 30.0.0); snapshot/testdata/rust/MANIFEST.json lists every file with its
  checksum. Known differences from the reference outputs are recorded in
  snapshot/rust_deviations_test.go.

Current scope
  Frontend: WGSL.
  Backends: SPIR-V, MSL, GLSL, HLSL; DXIL (experimental, not in Rust naga).
  Rust naga's SPIR-V and GLSL frontends and its WGSL and DOT outputs are not
  implemented.
